---
import '../styles/landing.css';
import '../styles/night-guide.css';
import logo from '../assets/orange/raven-orange-dark.svg';
import RavenHunt from '../components/RavenHunt.astro';
import SiteHead from '../components/SiteHead.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <SiteHead
      title="Code Mortis | Code review with evidence."
      description="Review Git changes, inspect the source behind each finding, and verify fixes with Mortis Engine and your choice of AI model."
      themeColor="#191b18"
    />
  </head>
  <body class="landing night-watch">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="page-width mast">
      <a href="/" aria-label="Code Mortis home"><img src={logo.src} alt="Code Mortis" width="173" height="30" /></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#inside-the-engine">Engine</a>
        <a href="/comparison/">Compare</a>
        <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
        <a href="#blog">Blog</a>
      </nav>
      <a class="mast-end" href="https://github.com/code-mortis/mortis-engine">GitHub ↗</a>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="page-width opener">
        <div class="pitch">
          <h1>Find the bug.<br /><em>Show the line.</em></h1>
          <p>Code review that points to the source. Mortis checks your Git changes for bugs and lets you verify the fix with the AI model you choose.</p>
          <div class="hero-links">
            <a class="install-link" href="#install">Install the Engine <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            <a class="text-link" href="#example-finding">Inspect a finding</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage"><RavenHunt scene="night-watch" facingLeft /></div>
      </section>
      <div class="feature-area" id="features">
        <div class="page-width">
          <section class="walkthrough" id="workflow">
            <h2>Follow one bug<br/><em>through a review.</em></h2>
            <ol>
              <li><div><h3>Choose the change</h3><p>Start with the index. Preview the scope before any source goes to your provider.</p><code>mortis review --staged --preview</code></div></li>
              <li id="example-finding"><div><h3>Read the evidence</h3><p>In this example, 21 items at 10 per page need three pages. Integer division counts only two.</p><code>pagination.py:18 · total // page_size</code></div></li>
              <li><div><h3>Check the fix</h3><p>Commit the correction, then verify the original finding against the new revision.</p><code>mortis verify --run RUN_ID --ref HEAD</code></div></li>
            </ol>
          </section>
          <section class="engine-features" id="inside-the-engine" aria-labelledby="engine-features-title">
            <h2 id="engine-features-title"><span id="engine">Inside the</span><br/><em>Engine.</em></h2>
            <ul class="engine-index">
              <li>
                <h3><a href="/docs/cli/#run-a-review">Code graph</a></h3>
                <p>The optional graph maps definitions and imports at the revision under review, giving Mortis context across files.</p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <h3><a href="/docs/cli/#scan-a-committed-revision">Security scans</a></h3>
                <p>Trivy checks dependencies, configuration, and secrets. Mortis assesses findings against the source and reports which files the scan covered.</p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <h3><a href="/docs/cli/#revisit-a-saved-run">Finding history</a></h3>
                <p>Record why you marked a false positive or accepted a risk. Later scans of the same scope carry the decision forward alongside the original evidence.</p>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
      <section class="page-width journal" id="blog">
        <div><h2>From the blog</h2><p>Engineering notes from Code Mortis.</p></div>
        <div class="story">
          <small>Proposed first article</small>
          <h3>What a code review can miss on the last page</h3>
          <p>How one boundary case changes what a reviewer should look for.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="install-band" id="install">
        <div class="page-width" id="get-started">
          <div><h2>Run your first review.</h2><p>Install the CLI, then run these commands from your Git repository.</p></div>
          <div>
            <pre><code>uv tool install mortis-engine{'\n'}mortis connect{'\n'}mortis review --progress</code></pre>
            <a class="text-link" href="/docs/cli/">CLI guide</a>
            <a class="text-link" href="/docs/library/">Python library guide</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="page-width">
      <a href="/"><img src={logo.src} width="140" height="24" alt="Code Mortis" /></a>
      <a href="/docs/">Documentation</a>
      <a href="#blog">Blog</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
